    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182-a4">

                <pb facs="0280" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg204"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Tsungli Yamen to the
                            Russian Legation
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1899-12-14">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi> 14, 1899</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On the 8th day of the 11th moon of the 25th year of Kuanghsu (December 10, 1899),
                    we received your note stating that you are glad to learn that China has not
                    agreed with any foreign company for the construction of the Peking-Kalgan
                    Railway, and that if it should be decided to construct this road, it will be
                    done in conformity with the stipulations of the note of the 23d day of the 4th
                    moon (June 1, 1899). This has been transmitted to the (Russian) Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <p>This Yamen (the Tsungli Yamen) has noted the above and now sends this formal
                    acknowledgement.</p>
            </div>
